#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# lexicographic_order

#% text
# `lexicographic_order(a, b)` compares the elements of `a` and `b` in turn with `order` and gives 1, -1 or 0 at the first difference; a list that is a prefix of the other comes first. Strings are compared by their characters, associations by their values. `lexicographic_order(a, b, p)` compares the elements with the ordering function `p`.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
lexicographic_order([a, b], [a, c])
#% output
#= 1

#% cell
lexicographic_order([a, b, c], [a, b])
#% output
#= -1

#% cell
lexicographic_order([2, 1], [10], numerical_order)
#% output
#= 1

